+
+## Policy change
+
+- Acceptance uses executable tests, explicit scope criteria, traceable artifacts, and the owner's recorded decision.
+- Existing SHA references, diffs, test logs, CI links, manifests, source-history references, and factual metadata remain available for traceability.
+- Historical evidence is preserved as originally recorded; this change does not rewrite commits or retroactively alter evidence.
+- Product readiness is assessed against actual external-impact and production criteria; this policy change does not itself certify readiness.
+- No merge, deployment, canonical mutation, branch deletion, or history rewrite is included.
+
+## Scope and state
+
+This proposal exists only on the isolated branch `governance/simplify-acceptance-policy-20261013`, forked locally from the candidate SHA. The canonical branch and existing candidate branch/PR are unchanged. External-consumer impact, production authentication, VPS/HTTPS/device end-to-end behavior, and real power-loss behavior remain separate open product criteria.
