+# HG2 Product Scope Acceptance — V1
+
+**State:** `ACCEPTANCE IN PROGRESS — BLOCKED / NO-GO`
+**Candidate branch:** `fix/hg2-single-product-readiness-20261013`
+**Baseline protected:** `hg-genesis` @ `d11e71ed8b34338b8568664b39bc777c926826d5`
+**Decision record:** `contract/PRODUCT_SCOPE_DECISIONS_V1.json`
+**Source inventory:** `evidence/HG2_PRODUCT_SCOPE_DEPENDENCY_INVENTORY_V1.json`
+
+## HTTP API scope — `PSD-API-001` (choice C)
+
+Read-only source inventory confirmed the legacy HG `runtime/hg_runtime/service.py` serves `GET /v1/history` and `POST /v1/sessions`; its tests and contracts are listed with immutable source commit, Git blob and SHA-256 references in the JSON inventory. The HG2 candidate does not ship that service module. Its `hg/edge.py` router exposes only `/health` and `/edge/*` routes. Acceptance tests exercise the candidate HTTP router and require all four method/path combinations for the legacy paths to return `404 NOT_FOUND`, without mutating edge state, while supported edge routes continue to work and authentication still fails closed.
+
+This proves behavior of the candidate router in a local integration test, not absence of unknown external clients or deployed copies. The read-only `OAI-GIANG/hg-ops` main tree at `2e75a6cbae2fa46e48ffa3fe67a134c385ee880e` was also searched, with no exact references found in its operational scripts, Nginx config or OpenAPI spec. External consumers/deployments are still not discoverable from repository source alone; this impact gate remains open until their status is independently established or explicitly accepted as a residual risk by the authorized owner.
+
+## Phone Bridge 1.1 scope — `PSD-BRIDGE-001` (choice C)
+
+The exact `OAI-GIANG/GO` branch `hg-phone-bridge-v1` was inspected at commit `4a20c319fe740f1a092ade4e407d693439629385`. It contains only `phone_bridge/README.md`, `bridge.py`, and `protocol.md`. The README calls the implementation a skeleton/not production; the protocol states staging-only and identifies production replay persistence, real governance/AEGR, durable execution, EvidenceLedger, device E2E and production transport as separate gates. A source-wide scan found no imports or references to the Bridge symbols outside that package on that branch. The read-only `OAI-GIANG/hg-ops` main tree at `2e75a6cbae2fa46e48ffa3fe67a134c385ee880e` also contained no exact Bridge symbol references. The HG2 candidate contains no Bridge module, protocol file, manifest entry or corresponding runtime symbols.
+
+The capability inventory covers request parsing, injected authentication, replay/time-window checks, authorization outcomes, governed execution submission, evidence correlation and safe errors. Tests assert that Bridge implementation/protocol symbols are not shipped in the HG2 runtime package and that the phone runtime remains fail-closed without a real verifier. This is intentional non-inclusion in HG2, not deletion of the original GO source, and not evidence that the bridge was production-ready or replaced. Unknown external consumers remain a residual risk.
+
+## Product identity — `PSD-ID-001` (choice A)
+
+`manifest.json` maps `product_id=HG` to `product_name=HG2`; runtime identity and event history retain `PRODUCT_ID="HG"`. New-store tests cover event records, replay, projection and audit export. A valid two-event store fixture was generated by extracting the exact canonical baseline implementation read-only at `d11e71ed8b34338b8568664b39bc777c926826d5`. The acceptance test copies that fixture, reopens and verifies it, and compares bytes of `history.jsonl`, `head.json`, `state.json` and `runtime_id` before/after to prove that reopening does not rewrite historical durable artifacts.
+
+## Acceptance IDs
+
+- `T-API-01`: legacy route/source inventory and candidate route behavior.
+- `T-API-02`: repository dependency inventory; external clients/deployments remain unknown and therefore block full impact closure.
+- `T-API-03`: candidate router integration test for `404 NOT_FOUND` on removed routes and continued operation of supported routes.
+- `T-API-04`: strict full-suite history, identity and authorization regression tests.
+- `T-BRIDGE-01`: exact Bridge source/protocol capability inventory.
+- `T-BRIDGE-02`: consumer search on available source branches; external consumers remain unknown.
+- `T-BRIDGE-03`: fail-closed phone authentication and history-integrity regression tests.
+- `T-BRIDGE-04`: runtime package/manifest static scan for Bridge implementation symbols.
+- `T-ID-01`: durable ID/product label mapping tests.
+- `T-ID-02`: fresh store create/replay/verify/audit export.
+- `T-ID-03`: reopen the pre-mapping canonical fixture and assert durable bytes are unchanged.
+- `T-ID-04`: identity/static-scan checks against unapproved HG-to-HG2 durable-ID conversion.
+
+## Evidence and release gates
+
+The test suite is evidence only for the exact source SHA executed. A clean checkout, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -W error::ResourceWarning -m unittest discover -s tests -v`, output log SHA-256 and successful CI status tied to the same commit are required. A test failure discovered during work must be recorded and fixed before acceptance. No source-tree grep is substituted for router integration tests.
+
+Known limits remain: external consumers are unknown; production authentication, VPS/HTTPS/device E2E and actual power-loss tests have not been performed. Historical evidence and metadata remain preserved as facts. Keep the overall status `BLOCKED / NO-GO` until the external-impact and production criteria are resolved.
+
+No merge, deployment, canonical mutation, repository/branch archive or deletion, or history rewrite is authorized.
+
+
+## Exact-SHA evidence snapshot
+
+`evidence/HG2_PRODUCT_SCOPE_ACCEPTANCE_EVIDENCE_74ECB9E.json` records clean-checkout results for source commit `74ecb9ef310008d07e2799b567e50b2ebd41f271`, 54/54 strict tests, log SHA-256 `d4571599a93253ee562ef70ce5dcca10c2e395070a3cd54851318ff051eb0cd8`, and CircleCI run #17. The evidence-record commit itself must be re-tested on its own exact SHA. This evidence does not close the external-consumer or production gates.
+
+
+## Updated exact-SHA evidence
+
+`evidence/HG2_PRODUCT_SCOPE_ACCEPTANCE_EVIDENCE_46E90FB.json` records clean-checkout results for source commit `46e90fb226e0c434158212a69717025745cad337`, including the read-only ops-repository inventory extension, 54/54 strict tests, log SHA-256 `1b687aeab6800f6d4f5e772793ccf6b1cad4e08d4e31ec63c10bd7ed40cfc1b6`, and CircleCI run #19. The evidence-record commit itself must be re-tested on its own exact SHA.
